the charge amplifier: C_f 10 pF, the input 20 pF; the ADC's step 50 uV
== the charge amplifier's output, peak, cable 3 cm deep
  50 Hz mains, 230 V           bone dry   717.317 mV  ordinary    23.131 mV  damp     0.231 mV
  a tracer, 10 V at 33 kHz     bone dry    31.118 mV  ordinary    39.156 mV  damp     6.579 mV
  a tracer, 10 V at 125 kHz    bone dry    31.118 mV  ordinary    32.160 mV  damp    22.379 mV
  from 231.4 uV to 717 mV: a range of 70 dB — so the gain is switched, not fixed
== what the op-amp must carry (gain-bandwidth product)
  GBW    1 MHz: the charge amplifier, noise gain 3, holds to  0.33 MHz; a second stage of gain 10 to    100 kHz, of gain 100 to    10 kHz
  GBW   10 MHz: the charge amplifier, noise gain 3, holds to  3.33 MHz; a second stage of gain 10 to   1000 kHz, of gain 100 to   100 kHz
  GBW   50 MHz: the charge amplifier, noise gain 3, holds to 16.67 MHz; a second stage of gain 10 to   5000 kHz, of gain 100 to   500 kHz
== the gain the weakest case wants before the ADC
  second stage x1  :     231.4 uV peak =    4.59 ADC steps; a narrow filter in software over 0.1 s at 125 kHz gains about 38 dB more
  second stage x10 :    2313.6 uV peak =   45.95 ADC steps; a narrow filter in software over 0.1 s at 125 kHz gains about 38 dB more
  second stage x100:   23135.9 uV peak =  459.47 ADC steps; a narrow filter in software over 0.1 s at 125 kHz gains about 38 dB more
